window.EN={"1":"Having defeated Priest-General Martel of Bern's Northern Army,","2":"what awaited Roy and the others as they broke through the forest","3":"was a blizzard of snow and ice unique to the Ilia region... a true blizzard.","4":"This harsh climate of Ilia, having turned back the invasions of outside enemies so many times before,","5":"had come to be called, with dread and reverence, the \"General Winter.\"","6":"That mightiest of Ilia's commanders, \"General Winter,\" together with the pegasus knight order Sigune Squadron, which had sided with Bern,","7":"now falls upon Roy and the others.","8":"Captain Sigune! A report has come in that the enemy has reached the far side of the mountain...","9":"So they've come. It's finally here, is it.","10":"...Captain Sigune. Is this really all right?","11":"What do you mean?","12":"The enemy claims to be liberating the continent from Bern's rule.","13":"If that's true, then Ilia's independence too...","14":"You—do you honestly believe what those people say?","15":"What fool fights a war for the sake of others? Where in the world does such a thing exist?","16":"Once they've beaten Bern, in the end they'll just turn around and think to rule over Ilia too.","17":"That may well be so, but...","18":"That's exactly why it's best to just go along with the stronger side. Bern is far better at war, after all.","19":".........","20":"If you have the spare time to worry about such things, spend it thinking about how to beat the enemy in front of you instead.","21":"Are the Shooters ready?","22":"Yes, the Archers are all in position.","23":"Hee hee hee... the enemy, caught in the blinding snow, won't even be able to see properly around them.","24":"Taste well the dread of Ilia's famous \"General Winter.\"","25":"What a terrible blizzard. With this, I can't see anything around us at all...","26":"Ho ho ho, Ilia's winters are always like this.","27":"Seeing as you're trying to wage a war in winter, there's no helping it.","28":"We can't very well afford to give Bern the chance to recover its footing...","29":"Well, that's certainly true.","30":"It would be a serious problem if the \"Dragon-Devil\" really has been revived.","31":"Niime, I wonder what sort of form the \"Dragon-Devil\" takes.","32":"Just like the \"dragons\" we've seen up till now, perhaps the \"Dragon-Devil\" too takes a human form?","33":"That's so.","34":"All the \"dragons\" may well be borrowing human form right now.","35":"I don't know if it's true or false, but","36":"I've at least heard tell that there are dragonkin living alongside humans in human form.","37":"The village of Nabata...","38":"Hm? Did you say something?","39":"No, it's nothing.","40":"I don't know the details, but after the \"Ending Winter,\"","41":"dragons are said to have begun taking human form, or so I've seen in an old document.","42":"The \"Ending Winter\"...","43":"You've at least heard of it, haven't you?","44":"Yes, I learned of it as a legend.","45":"\"At that time, the world's 'order' went mad,","46":"day became night, summer became winter,","47":"and heaven and earth raged as if to reject all living things,\" or so it's told.","48":"That's right. It's such an old thing that accounts differ depending on the text,","49":"but in any case, the \"Ending Winter\" was a great calamity that changed the world.","50":"What was the cause?","51":"Well now...","52":"By one account, it's said that the \"dragons\" used a vast amount of magical power,","53":"and that this warped the order of nature, but the truth of the matter I don't know either.","54":"However, it does seem certain that it was after this that \"dragons\" began taking human form.","55":"I can't think it's entirely unrelated.","56":"Yes, indeed, that does seem true.","57":"Well, in any case, it seems the truth about \"dragons\" lies with Bern.","58":"To think anyone would come all the way out to a remote place like this...","59":"So then... the prophecy was right after all.","60":"The world now is like a storm swirling outside... the light still cannot be seen...","61":"This tome is a single gust of wind that will clear away that dark cloud.","62":"And you all, surely... are the single ray of light that shines down into it.","63":"Do I keep living, following along with Bern... or...","64":"I've agonized over it for so long... but at last my heart is made up.","65":"I'll give this to you.","66":"This is a ring that awakens the power of the inner fight.","67":"They say if you use it, you can gain tremendous power.","68":"Please... bring peace to this land...","69":"The Bern army's stronghold here in Ilia...? Um, let me think, I believe it was Eda... Ere...","70":"Ede— a castle called Edessa, I believe. It's said to be northeast of here.","71":"The Shooters to the east, do you know about them? Here should still be fine, though.","72":"I think the item shop nearby is dangerous...","73":"Pegasus knights, and Shooters too...","74":"Ilia's Sigune has her sights set on you all.","75":"Deep within the blizzard, holding her breath, waiting.","76":"You all are out of luck too.","77":"Guarding this place is the \"White Devil\"—the Sigune Squadron.","78":"Ilia's pegasi fly even through this blizzard.","79":"They suddenly appear right before your eyes, out of the white snow.","80":"By the time you notice them, it's already too late...","81":"Ah... just thinking about it makes me shiver...!","82":"※If Sigune survives only","83":"Captain! Some of the pegasus knights from other units","84":"have reported that they're heading this way to help us!","85":"Is that so? That's quite welcome news.","86":"If, in this unfamiliar blizzard, we were suddenly attacked from all sides...","87":"Hee hee hee. The enemy would be in quite a pitiable state.","88":"※If fought with Shanna: You're Juno's youngest sister, aren't you.","89":"Are you saying you'll be my opponent?","90":".........","91":"The Ilia knight's oath... I won't go easy on you, understand?","92":"Mm...","93":"※If fought with Thea: Oh, isn't that Thea? What are you doing here...","94":"I see, so you've sided with Etruria...","95":"Sigune...","96":"You remember the Ilia knight's oath, don't you?","97":"I won't hold back.","98":"※If fought with any other unit: You've worked hard in this cold, haven't you? But that's over now...","99":"This is the end of the line for you all...","100":"...How unfair. So it's me who ends up dying...","101":"No... perhaps I died a long, long time ago...","102":"Marinas, I'd like you to send this letter to Bern's Priest Yodel.","103":"A letter...? May I ask what it says?","104":"It's something I heard from Niime. About the \"dragons\" Bern makes use of.","105":"Oh! Whatever sort of talk did you have?","106":"It would take a while to explain, so...","107":"I haven't sealed it yet, so it'd be best if you just read over the letter yourself.","108":"Understood. Well then, let me have a look right away...","109":"...Lord Roy.","110":"Princess Guinevere. What's the matter?","111":"Would you listen... to something I have to say, about my brother?","112":"!! ...Are you sure you want to tell me?","113":"Yes... after all, I feel you ought to know, before we enter Bern.","114":"About the dreadful thing that happened within the Bern royal family.","115":"...The other day, you asked whether my brother—whether King Zephiel of Bern—","116":"had laid hands on our father, the former king.","117":"Yes...","118":"To give you the conclusion first... it's true.","119":"! Then King Zephiel truly did, aiming for the throne, lay hands on his own father...","120":"That's not it!","121":"Not it? Then didn't he assassinate the former king for the sake of the throne?","122":"That's not it... it was Father, first, who plotted the assassination.","123":"What! Th-then King Zephiel...","124":"Unable to bear Father's tyrannical conduct any longer, he... he took Father's life with his own hands...","125":"What in the world...","126":"...My, \"dragons\" truly are mysterious creatures, aren't they...","127":"Hm? Is something the matter, you two?","128":"No... it's... we'll speak of it again sometime...","129":"...Could it be that my coming here just now was poorly timed?","130":"No, that's not it at all. More to the point, did you send it off for me? The letter.","131":"Yes. After I read it through, I sealed it and sent it off right away...","132":"I see. Thank you.","133":"Bern's former king... why would he do that, to his own true son..."};
